# Lovelace and kiosk stay in sync

Two dashboards show the same house. A change to a shared section goes to both in the same change, then both are deployed.

| | Regular (Lovelace) | Lightweight (kiosk) |
|---|---|---|
| Infrastructure | `homeassistant/dashboards/infrastructure.yaml` | `homeassistant/www/infra-kiosk/index.html` and `infrastructure.js` |
| Backyard | `homeassistant/dashboards/backyard.yaml` | `homeassistant/www/infra-kiosk/backyard.html` and `backyard.js` |

Shared sections today: core network, WAN map, power watchdogs, servers / NVR / GPU, camera health, storage, backyard surveillance, environment and soil, lighting, irrigation. A section that exists on only one dashboard stays there.

Shared cards (the WAN map is `custom:wan-connections-map`, loaded from `/wan_connections_map/wan-connections-map.js`) are one implementation. After a card change:

1. Bump `CARD_URL` in the card integration and the kiosk `<script src>` to the same `?v=` value.
2. Put the new bundle on the HA host and sync `homeassistant/www/`.
3. Confirm the Lovelace resource the regular dashboard loads is that same URL. The kiosk picking up a new file while Lovelace is still on the previous `?v=` is an unfinished change.

Canonical kiosk files are the ones listed above. Leave `homeassistant/www/infra-kiosk/infra-kiosk/` alone unless a page is actually served from there.
